1
00:00:01,293 --> 00:00:02,670
SO, NOW, WHAT
IS THIS NOW?

2
00:00:02,711 --> 00:00:03,671
GOOGILY WORM.

3
00:00:03,712 --> 00:00:05,172
( giggles )

4
00:00:05,213 --> 00:00:06,340
AND THIS?

5
00:00:06,381 --> 00:00:07,925
GLOW POP JIGGLY JAMMER.

6
00:00:07,967 --> 00:00:09,092
( laughs )

7
00:00:09,134 --> 00:00:10,928
BAIT IS SO FUNNY.

8
00:00:12,179 --> 00:00:15,014
HEY, UM, WHAT'S THIS?

9
00:00:15,056 --> 00:00:17,309
OH, A HUNK OF SANDWICH
FROM LAST YEAR.

10
00:00:18,894 --> 00:00:20,437
OH, GELLER'S GOT ONE HOOKED.

11
00:00:20,479 --> 00:00:21,897
OH! LOOKS LIKE A BIG ONE!

12
00:00:21,939 --> 00:00:27,569
UH-OH, IT'S THE CLASSIC STRUGGLE
BETWEEN MAN AND...

13
00:00:29,404 --> 00:00:31,198
SOMEONE KNOCKED OVER A LAMP.

14
00:00:31,239 --> 00:00:34,075
HEY, YOU GUYS, YOU KNOW
WHAT'S GOING TO BE GREAT

15
00:00:34,117 --> 00:00:36,077
ABOUT THE FISHING TRIP
THIS YEAR?

16
00:00:36,119 --> 00:00:37,579
WHEN MY DAD
GIVES ME THAT

17
00:00:37,621 --> 00:00:39,957
"JOEY, WHAT ARE
YOU DOING WITH
YOUR LIFE?" STUFF

18
00:00:39,999 --> 00:00:41,834
I CAN SAY, "WELL,
I'M DOING A MOVIE

19
00:00:41,876 --> 00:00:43,335
"WITH CHARLTON
HESTON, DAD.

20
00:00:43,377 --> 00:00:45,212
WHAT ARE YOU DOING
WITH YOUR LIFE?"

21
00:00:45,253 --> 00:00:47,255
( quacking )

22
00:00:49,842 --> 00:00:52,887
YOU DON'T HAVE TO STOP HAVING
FUN JUST BECAUSE I'M HERE.

23
00:00:52,928 --> 00:00:55,347
KATHY DIDN'T CHEAT
ON ALL OF YOU.

24
00:00:56,682 --> 00:00:58,517
WELL, EXCEPT YOU.

25
00:01:04,982 --> 00:01:08,235
( quacking )

26
00:01:08,276 --> 00:01:09,904
Monica:
HEY, JOEY, I DON'T THINK

27
00:01:09,945 --> 00:01:11,279
YOU SHOULD LEAVE CHANDLER ALONE.

28
00:01:11,321 --> 00:01:12,155
IT'S ONLY BEEN TWO DAYS

29
00:01:12,197 --> 00:01:13,532
SINCE HE BROKE UP
WITH KATHY.

30
00:01:13,574 --> 00:01:14,700
MAYBE YOU CAN GO
FISHING NEXT WEEK.

31
00:01:14,742 --> 00:01:16,744
THERE'S NOTHING I
CAN DO FOR HIM NOW.

32
00:01:16,785 --> 00:01:18,453
HE'S STILL IN
HIS SWEAT PANTS.

33
00:01:18,495 --> 00:01:19,955
THAT'S ONLY PHASE ONE.

34
00:01:19,997 --> 00:01:22,374
YOU KNOW,
I'LL BE BACK
FOR PHASE TWO.

35
00:01:22,416 --> 00:01:24,376
I WOULD NEVER
MISS PHASE TWO.

36
00:01:24,418 --> 00:01:26,127
WHAT'S PHASE TWO?

37
00:01:26,169 --> 00:01:28,422
GETTING DRUNK AND
GOING TO A STRIP CLUB.

38
00:01:30,007 --> 00:01:31,884
HOW DOES GOING
TO A STRIP CLUB

39
00:01:31,926 --> 00:01:33,218
MAKE HIM BETTER?

40
00:01:33,260 --> 00:01:34,762
THERE ARE NAKED LADIES THERE.

41
00:01:34,803 --> 00:01:36,471
IT HELPS HIM GET
TO PHASE THREE:

42
00:01:36,513 --> 00:01:38,515
"PICTURING YOURSELF
WITH OTHER WOMEN."

43
00:01:38,557 --> 00:01:40,350
THERE ARE NAKED LADIES
THERE, TOO.

44
00:01:40,392 --> 00:01:41,936
YEAH.

45
00:01:41,977 --> 00:01:43,144
( quacking )

46
00:01:43,186 --> 00:01:45,188
WOULD YOU GIVE ME
ONE MINUTE, PLEASE?

47
00:01:52,780 --> 00:01:57,618
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

48
00:01:57,659 --> 00:02:00,119
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

49
00:02:00,161 --> 00:02:02,497
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

50
00:02:02,539 --> 00:02:07,461
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

51
00:02:07,502 --> 00:02:09,046
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN YOUR DAY ♪

52
00:02:09,088 --> 00:02:12,716
♪ YOUR WEEK, YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

53
00:02:12,758 --> 00:02:16,553
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

54
00:02:16,595 --> 00:02:17,679
♪ WHEN THE RAIN
STARTS TO POUR ♪

55
00:02:17,721 --> 00:02:20,390
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

56
00:02:20,432 --> 00:02:22,810
♪ LIKE I'VE BEEN THERE BEFORE ♪

57
00:02:22,851 --> 00:02:26,105
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

58
00:02:26,187 --> 00:02:28,315
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

59
00:02:38,117 --> 00:02:40,410
THESE WILL MATCH THE JACKET
YOU PICKED OUT FOR ME?

60
00:02:40,452 --> 00:02:41,703
MM-HMM.

61
00:02:41,745 --> 00:02:44,205
THERE WE GO.

62
00:02:44,247 --> 00:02:45,874
THERE IT IS.

63
00:02:45,916 --> 00:02:47,375
OH, YOU KNOW WHAT I NEED?

64
00:02:47,417 --> 00:02:48,543
YEAH?

65
00:02:48,585 --> 00:02:49,670
GLOVES.

66
00:02:49,711 --> 00:02:51,296
BROWN LEATHER DRESS GLOVES.

67
00:02:51,338 --> 00:02:53,214
OH, OKAY, UH,
WELL, LET'S SEE.

68
00:02:53,256 --> 00:02:54,591
YOU'RE ABOUT A, WELL

69
00:02:54,633 --> 00:02:56,093
THIS ONE IS LARGE.

70
00:02:56,135 --> 00:02:58,095
AND, UH, THIS ONE...

71
00:02:58,137 --> 00:02:59,346
ALSO LARGE?

72
00:02:59,387 --> 00:03:00,514
YEAH. OKAY.

73
00:03:00,555 --> 00:03:02,181
TWO LARGES COMING RIGHT UP.

74
00:03:02,223 --> 00:03:03,517
OKAY.

75
00:03:03,558 --> 00:03:05,184
( scoffs )

76
00:03:05,226 --> 00:03:06,979
RACHEL, COULD I HAVE A MOMENT?

77
00:03:07,021 --> 00:03:07,980
YES.

78
00:03:08,022 --> 00:03:09,272
I WAS WONDERING...

79
00:03:09,314 --> 00:03:11,692
MY NIECE, YOU SEE,
IS IN TOWN FROM LONDON.

80
00:03:11,733 --> 00:03:13,527
SHROPSHIRE, REALLY,
BUT YOU KNOW...

81
00:03:13,568 --> 00:03:15,904
WELL, SHE'S ABOUT YOUR AGE,
I'D SAY.

82
00:03:15,946 --> 00:03:18,782
ANYWAY, I HAVE TICKETS
FOR THE OPERA, DIE FLEDERMAUS

83
00:03:18,824 --> 00:03:20,784
AND I WAS WONDERING
IF YOU WOULD LIKE

84
00:03:20,826 --> 00:03:22,619
TO KEEP HER COMPANY
THIS EVENING.

85
00:03:22,661 --> 00:03:23,704
SURE, YOU GOT IT.

86
00:03:23,745 --> 00:03:24,872
GREAT. COUNT ME IN.

87
00:03:24,913 --> 00:03:26,081
ME, FLEDERMAUS, GREAT.

88
00:03:26,123 --> 00:03:27,082
I REALLY...

89
00:03:27,124 --> 00:03:28,458
HMM? OH, YES, OF COURSE.

90
00:03:28,500 --> 00:03:29,459
THANK YOU.

91
00:03:29,501 --> 00:03:31,795
THANK YOU
SO VERY MUCH.

92
00:03:31,837 --> 00:03:33,755
SO?

93
00:03:35,883 --> 00:03:37,176
SO?

94
00:03:40,846 --> 00:03:42,221
GLOVES?

95
00:03:42,263 --> 00:03:43,891
OH, RIGHT, I'LL
BE RIGHT BACK.

96
00:03:43,932 --> 00:03:45,184
ACTUALLY,
YOU KNOW WHAT?

97
00:03:45,225 --> 00:03:46,894
I KIND OF...
I GOT TO TAKE OFF

98
00:03:46,935 --> 00:03:48,062
BUT I WAS CURIOUS...

99
00:03:48,103 --> 00:03:49,980
DO YOU HAVE ANY
PLANS FOR TONIGHT?

100
00:03:50,022 --> 00:03:52,066
NO. NOTHING!

101
00:03:52,107 --> 00:03:55,069
I INVESTED IN THIS NIGHTCLUB
AND IT'S OPENING TONIGHT.

102
00:03:55,110 --> 00:03:57,196
YEAH, THAT WOULD BE GREAT.

103
00:03:57,237 --> 00:03:59,322
YOU'RE INTO HARD-CORE
S&amp;M, RIGHT?

104
00:04:01,867 --> 00:04:03,368
WELL, I-I GU... I GUE...

105
00:04:03,410 --> 00:04:04,244
I'M KIDDING.

106
00:04:04,285 --> 00:04:05,244
( chuckles )

107
00:04:05,286 --> 00:04:06,245
WHEW!

108
00:04:06,287 --> 00:04:07,664
I GOT TO GET
THERE EARLY

109
00:04:07,706 --> 00:04:09,791
BUT I'M GOING
TO PUT YOU ON
THE V.I.P. LIST.

110
00:04:09,833 --> 00:04:10,792
LOOK FOR ME.

111
00:04:10,834 --> 00:04:11,793
YEAH. GREAT.

112
00:04:11,835 --> 00:04:13,628
I'LL SEE YOU TONIGHT.
OKAY.

113
00:04:13,670 --> 00:04:16,464
I ALMOST FORGOT THE
TICKETS, DIDN'T I?

114
00:04:16,506 --> 00:04:17,632
WHAT?

115
00:04:17,674 --> 00:04:18,800
FOR YOU AND EMILY.

116
00:04:18,842 --> 00:04:19,801
TONIGHT.

117
00:04:19,843 --> 00:04:21,136
DIE FLEDERMAUS.

118
00:04:21,178 --> 00:04:24,598
OH... OH, RIGHT.

119
00:04:24,639 --> 00:04:25,599
I THINK
YOU'LL LIKE IT.

120
00:04:25,640 --> 00:04:27,226
IT HAS TWO OUT OF
THE THREE TENORS.

121
00:04:27,267 --> 00:04:29,853
OH, YAY!

122
00:04:33,899 --> 00:04:36,526
YOU KNOW, I CAN'T BELIEVE
KATHY DID THIS TO ME.

123
00:04:36,568 --> 00:04:38,820
I REALLY THOUGHT
THAT SHE WAS THE ONE.

124
00:04:38,862 --> 00:04:40,530
WELL, I'LL TELL YOU WHAT.

125
00:04:40,572 --> 00:04:44,118
FROM NOW ON, I'M NOT GETTING
OUT OF THIS CHAIR EVER, OKAY?

126
00:04:44,159 --> 00:04:46,327
FROM NOW ON,
THIS CHAIR IS "THE ONE."

127
00:04:46,369 --> 00:04:48,329
YOU KNOW WHAT ELSE
IS "THE ONE"?

128
00:04:48,371 --> 00:04:49,330
MY SWEAT PANTS.

129
00:04:49,372 --> 00:04:50,665
COME ON, MAN

130
00:04:50,707 --> 00:04:54,377
JUST-JUST TAKE THE
SWEATS OFF, OKAY?

131
00:04:54,419 --> 00:04:57,005
JUST TAKE 'EM OFF,
AND WE'LL HAVE SOME FUN.

132
00:05:00,008 --> 00:05:01,260
HEY, HEY.

133
00:05:01,301 --> 00:05:02,427
HI.
HI.

134
00:05:02,469 --> 00:05:04,012
HAVE A GOOD TIME?
CATCH A BIG ONE?

135
00:05:04,054 --> 00:05:06,181
OH, GOD,
YOU GUYS HAVE NO IDEA.

136
00:05:06,223 --> 00:05:07,182
WOW, YOU STINK!

137
00:05:07,224 --> 00:05:08,558
ARE YOU KIDDING?

138
00:05:08,600 --> 00:05:10,894
YEAH, THREE DAYS ON THE LAKE
WITHOUT A SHOWER.

139
00:05:10,936 --> 00:05:14,231
PLUS, I FELL INTO THAT BIG
TUB OF WORMS AT THE BAIT STAND.

140
00:05:16,108 --> 00:05:17,442
HEY, H-HOW'S HE DOING?

141
00:05:17,484 --> 00:05:19,736
HE HASN'T MOVED IN TWO DAYS.

142
00:05:19,778 --> 00:05:22,322
HEY, BUDDY, HOW'S IT GOING?

143
00:05:27,911 --> 00:05:29,037
HEY, YOU SEE THAT?

144
00:05:29,079 --> 00:05:30,914
HE JUST NEEDED HIS PAL
TO COME HOME.

145
00:05:30,956 --> 00:05:33,125
ALL RIGHT, I GOT TO
GO MEMORIZE MY LINES.

146
00:05:33,167 --> 00:05:36,211
ME AND CHARLTON HESTON,
BRIGHT AND EARLY TOMORROW, BABY!

147
00:05:36,253 --> 00:05:37,378
YEAH, YOU DO 'EM!

148
00:05:37,420 --> 00:05:38,546
HEY.

149
00:05:38,588 --> 00:05:40,048
Ross:
HEY.

150
00:05:40,090 --> 00:05:41,382
Phoebe:
HEY, MONICA.

151
00:05:41,424 --> 00:05:43,551
UH-OH, WHAT'S THE MATTER?

152
00:05:43,593 --> 00:05:45,137
OH, IT'S...

153
00:05:45,179 --> 00:05:49,057
JOSHUA INVITED ME
TO THIS FANCY CLUB
OPENING TONIGHT.

154
00:05:49,099 --> 00:05:51,643
OOH, BUT I ALREADY
TOLD MR. WALTHAM

155
00:05:51,685 --> 00:05:53,645
THAT I WOULD
TAKE HIS NIECE

156
00:05:53,687 --> 00:05:56,982
TO THE DUMB
OLD OPERA, SO...

157
00:05:57,024 --> 00:05:59,318
WHAT ARE YOU
GOING TO DO?

158
00:05:59,358 --> 00:06:00,652
( sighs )

159
00:06:00,694 --> 00:06:01,987
I DON'T KNOW, SWEETIE.

160
00:06:02,029 --> 00:06:03,362
NO! HELP ME!

161
00:06:03,404 --> 00:06:05,282
I CAN'T.
I HAVE TO WORK.

162
00:06:05,324 --> 00:06:06,741
PHOEBE...?

163
00:06:06,783 --> 00:06:09,203
I WOULD, BUT I GET
MORNING SICKNESS IN THE EVENING.

164
00:06:09,244 --> 00:06:11,246
UNLESS... SHE WANTS
TO SPEND THE NIGHT

165
00:06:11,288 --> 00:06:13,540
HOLDING MY HAIR BACK FOR ME.

166
00:06:13,581 --> 00:06:15,542
OH, GOSH, YOU GUYS, COME ON.

167
00:06:15,583 --> 00:06:17,585
THIS IS... I HAVE
TO MEET JOSHUA.

168
00:06:17,627 --> 00:06:20,755
THIS IS MY ONE CHANCE
FOR HIM TO SEE THE FUN RACHEL.

169
00:06:20,797 --> 00:06:22,924
YOU KNOW,
THE WOULDN'T-IT-BE-GREAT-

170
00:06:22,966 --> 00:06:24,634
IF-SHE-WERE-MY-WIFE RACHEL?

171
00:06:24,676 --> 00:06:26,803
OH, ALL RIGHT.

172
00:06:26,845 --> 00:06:28,471
ARE JOEY AND CHANDLER BACK?

173
00:06:28,513 --> 00:06:30,098
CHANDLER'S STILL IN PHASE ONE

174
00:06:30,140 --> 00:06:31,808
AND JOEY'S
THAT THING YOU SMELL.

175
00:06:31,850 --> 00:06:33,894
OH, THAT'S...

176
00:06:36,479 --> 00:06:38,899
HI.

177
00:06:39,941 --> 00:06:42,027
HI.

178
00:06:43,486 --> 00:06:45,697
SO...?

179
00:06:47,824 --> 00:06:49,117
NO.

180
00:06:49,159 --> 00:06:51,078
OH, COME ON.

181
00:06:51,119 --> 00:06:53,038
( knocking )

182
00:06:53,080 --> 00:06:54,622
BET SHE'S HERE.

183
00:06:54,664 --> 00:06:56,791
NO, WAIT, WAIT, WAIT.
ROSS, PLEASE!

184
00:06:56,833 --> 00:07:01,004
YOU WANT ME TO TAKE SOME GIRL
I'VE NEVER MET TO THE OPERA

185
00:07:01,046 --> 00:07:04,966
SO YOU CAN GO TO A CLUB
AND FLIRT WITH SOME GUY? HMM.

186
00:07:05,008 --> 00:07:07,177
YEAH, THAT-THAT IS A TOUGHIE...

187
00:07:07,219 --> 00:07:08,595
OH, SHE'S LOOKING

188
00:07:08,636 --> 00:07:09,596
DOWN THE HALL.

189
00:07:09,637 --> 00:07:10,597
( gasps )

190
00:07:10,638 --> 00:07:12,140
SHE LOOKED RIGHT AT ME.

191
00:07:12,182 --> 00:07:15,143
OH, WAIT, YOU CAN'T SEE PEOPLE
THROUGH THAT LITTLE HOLE

192
00:07:15,185 --> 00:07:16,353
CAN YOU?

193
00:07:17,354 --> 00:07:19,147
HELLO?

194
00:07:19,189 --> 00:07:20,315
Woman:
HELLO?

195
00:07:20,357 --> 00:07:22,609
( shrieks )

196
00:07:22,650 --> 00:07:23,902
OH, I'LL BE RIGHT THERE.

197
00:07:23,944 --> 00:07:25,362
OKAY, ROSS,
PLEASE COME ON.

198
00:07:25,404 --> 00:07:26,780
I THOUGHT WE HAD MOVED ON.

199
00:07:26,821 --> 00:07:28,573
I THOUGHT WE HAD GOTTEN
TO A PLACE

200
00:07:28,615 --> 00:07:30,658
WHERE WE COULD BE HAPPY
FOR EACH OTHER.

201
00:07:30,700 --> 00:07:31,868
WAS THAT JUST ME?

202
00:07:31,910 --> 00:07:34,371
ALL RIGHT, I'LL DO IT.

203
00:07:34,413 --> 00:07:35,622
OH, THANK YOU.

204
00:07:35,663 --> 00:07:37,498
THANK YOU, THANK YOU,
THANK YOU!

205
00:07:37,540 --> 00:07:38,833
EMILY?

206
00:07:38,875 --> 00:07:40,127
OH, YES.

207
00:07:40,168 --> 00:07:41,460
I'M RACHEL GREEN.

208
00:07:41,502 --> 00:07:43,213
THANK GOODNESS.
YEAH.

209
00:07:43,255 --> 00:07:45,673
THERE'S BEEN A TEENY,
TEENY CHANGE OF PLANS.

210
00:07:45,715 --> 00:07:47,717
TURNS OUT I'M NOT
FREE TONIGHT, SO...

211
00:07:47,759 --> 00:07:50,220
REALLY? WELL,
THAT'S JUST LOVELY, ISN'T IT?

212
00:07:50,262 --> 00:07:51,888
I MUST HAVE MISSED YOUR CALL

213
00:07:51,930 --> 00:07:54,515
EVEN THOUGH I DIDN'T
LEAVE THE FLAT ALL DAY.

214
00:07:54,557 --> 00:07:55,809
OH, WELL, NO, I...

215
00:07:55,850 --> 00:07:57,269
NO, NO, NO,
THAT'S NOT RUDE.

216
00:07:57,311 --> 00:07:59,354
IT'S PERFECTLY IN KEEPING
WITH THE TRIP

217
00:07:59,396 --> 00:08:01,398
WHERE I'VE ALREADY
BEEN RUN DOWN BY ONE

218
00:08:01,440 --> 00:08:02,607
OF YOUR WIENER CARS

219
00:08:02,649 --> 00:08:03,858
AND BEEN STRIP-SEARCHED

220
00:08:03,900 --> 00:08:05,319
AT JOHN F. KENNEDY AIRPORT.

221
00:08:05,360 --> 00:08:06,903
APPARENTLY TO YOU PEOPLE

222
00:08:06,945 --> 00:08:09,656
I LOOK LIKE SOMEONE WHO'S GOT
A BALLOON FULL OF COCAINE

223
00:08:09,697 --> 00:08:11,741
STUFFED UP THEIR BUM.

224
00:08:11,783 --> 00:08:15,996
I-I-I THINK YOU LOOK GREAT.

225
00:08:16,037 --> 00:08:17,496
GOOD NIGHT.

226
00:08:17,538 --> 00:08:19,540
IT WAS VERY NICE
TO MEET YOU ALL.

227
00:08:22,169 --> 00:08:23,586
I'LL GET HER.

228
00:08:23,628 --> 00:08:26,131
PLEASE, HURRY.

229
00:08:28,383 --> 00:08:30,551
SO, DON'T YOU JUST LOVE
THE WAY THEY TALK?

230
00:08:30,593 --> 00:08:32,929
"OOH..." UH, YOU KNOW...

231
00:08:39,436 --> 00:08:40,561
OH!

232
00:08:40,603 --> 00:08:41,646
WHAT?

233
00:08:41,688 --> 00:08:43,398
I THINK THE BABY KICKED.

234
00:08:43,440 --> 00:08:44,399
OH, MY GOD!

235
00:08:44,441 --> 00:08:45,442
( laughs )

236
00:08:45,484 --> 00:08:47,194
OH, NO, WAIT, OH,
THAT WAS THE ELASTIC

237
00:08:47,235 --> 00:08:49,070
IN MY UNDERWEAR BUSTED.

238
00:08:50,322 --> 00:08:51,865
MY GOD! I OVERSLEPT!

239
00:08:51,906 --> 00:08:54,409
I WAS SUPPOSED TO BE ON THE SET
A HALF AN HOUR AGO!

240
00:08:54,451 --> 00:08:55,785
I GOT TO GET OUT OF HERE!

241
00:08:55,827 --> 00:08:57,578
OH, JOEY, YOU
CAN'T GO LIKE THAT.

242
00:08:57,620 --> 00:08:58,913
YOU STINK!

243
00:08:58,955 --> 00:09:01,208
I FELL ASLEEP
BEFORE I COULD TAKE A SHOWER.

244
00:09:01,249 --> 00:09:02,917
THEY'RE JUST TEN BLOCKS AWAY.

245
00:09:02,959 --> 00:09:04,336
IF I RUN, I CAN MAKE IT.

246
00:09:04,378 --> 00:09:06,129
YEAH, RUN TEN BLOCKS.

247
00:09:06,171 --> 00:09:07,588
THAT'LL HELP
THE SMELL.

248
00:09:07,630 --> 00:09:08,965
HEY! OH! SLOW DOWN.

249
00:09:09,007 --> 00:09:10,591
NO, KEEP MOVING.

250
00:09:10,633 --> 00:09:12,760
SO, HOW DID IT GO
WITH JOSHUA LAST NIGHT?

251
00:09:12,802 --> 00:09:15,889
OH, WELL,
I DIDN'T SEE JOSHUA

252
00:09:15,930 --> 00:09:17,974
BUT I DID PUNCH A GIRL
IN THE FACE.

253
00:09:18,016 --> 00:09:19,100
WHAT?

254
00:09:19,142 --> 00:09:20,143
WHY?

255
00:09:20,185 --> 00:09:21,811
IT WAS POURING DOWN RAIN

256
00:09:21,853 --> 00:09:25,065
AND WHEN I GOT THERE, THERE WAS
NO RACHEL GREEN ON THE LIST

257
00:09:25,106 --> 00:09:26,941
BUT THERE WAS A RACHEL "GREEP."

258
00:09:26,983 --> 00:09:28,860
OH, SO DID YOU GET
TO MEET HER?

259
00:09:32,113 --> 00:09:34,199
NO, THERE IS NO RACHEL GREEP

260
00:09:34,241 --> 00:09:35,992
BUT THEN THIS OTHER GIRL
OVERHEARD US

261
00:09:36,034 --> 00:09:37,202
AND SHE WAS ALL,
"I'M RACHEL GREEP!

262
00:09:37,244 --> 00:09:38,036
I'M RACHEL GREEP!"

263
00:09:38,078 --> 00:09:39,287
AND HE LET HER RIGHT IN.

264
00:09:39,329 --> 00:09:40,830
SO YOU HIT HER
IN THE FACE?

265
00:09:40,872 --> 00:09:42,123
NO, SHE WAS ALREADY IN

266
00:09:42,165 --> 00:09:44,042
BUT THEN THIS BIG BITCH
BEHIND ME

267
00:09:44,084 --> 00:09:46,669
TRIED TO STEAL MY UMBRELLA,
SO I CLOCKED HER.

268
00:09:46,711 --> 00:09:49,672
OH! I CAN'T BELIEVE THIS.

269
00:09:49,714 --> 00:09:51,466
ALL I WANTED WAS JUST

270
00:09:51,508 --> 00:09:54,052
A FEW HOURS OUTSIDE OF WORK
TO SEE JOSHUA

271
00:09:54,094 --> 00:09:59,433
SO THAT HE COULD GO AHEAD AND
START FALLING IN LOVE WITH ME.

272
00:09:59,474 --> 00:10:00,934
OH...

273
00:10:00,975 --> 00:10:03,144
PHEEBS.

274
00:10:04,979 --> 00:10:06,814
HONEY, THAT'S YOUR NAME.

275
00:10:08,108 --> 00:10:09,317
THAT'S SHORT FOR PHOEBE?!

276
00:10:09,359 --> 00:10:11,069
I THOUGHT THAT'S
JUST WHAT WE CALLED EACH OTHER.

277
00:10:13,572 --> 00:10:15,990
Monica:
HEY, YOU'RE WEARING PANTS.

278
00:10:16,032 --> 00:10:17,325
THAT'S RIGHT.

279
00:10:17,367 --> 00:10:18,659
WHERE ARE THE GUYS?

280
00:10:18,701 --> 00:10:20,370
I'M READY TO GET DRUNK

281
00:10:20,412 --> 00:10:21,580
AND SEE
SOME STRIPPERS.

282
00:10:21,621 --> 00:10:22,997
IT'S 9:30 IN THE MORNING.

283
00:10:23,039 --> 00:10:25,041
THEY GOT A BREAKFAST BUFFET.

284
00:10:25,083 --> 00:10:27,752
( phone rings )

285
00:10:27,794 --> 00:10:29,588
HELLO? OH, HEY, ROSS.

286
00:10:29,629 --> 00:10:31,005
OOH! LET ME
TALK TO HIM.

287
00:10:31,047 --> 00:10:31,798
OH, MY GOD!

288
00:10:31,839 --> 00:10:32,340
WELL, CAN I JUST...?

289
00:10:32,382 --> 00:10:33,341
SHH! WAIT, WHAT?

290
00:10:33,383 --> 00:10:34,509
SHE'S SHUSHING ME.

291
00:10:34,551 --> 00:10:35,718
SHH! PLEASE!

292
00:10:35,760 --> 00:10:37,304
WHAT'S HE SAYING?

293
00:10:37,345 --> 00:10:40,014
HE'S WITH EMILY AT A BED
AND BREAKFAST IN VERMONT.

294
00:10:40,056 --> 00:10:42,100
WHAT? OH, MY GOD!

295
00:10:42,142 --> 00:10:43,602
WHAT? WHO THE HELL IS EMILY?

296
00:10:43,642 --> 00:10:45,937
NO!

297
00:10:48,982 --> 00:10:51,025
HOW DID THIS HAPPEN?
OW.

298
00:10:51,067 --> 00:10:52,277
HOW-HOW DID HE END UP

299
00:10:52,319 --> 00:10:55,322
IN VERMONT WITH
THAT AWFUL WITCH?

300
00:10:55,363 --> 00:10:57,865
WELL, MAYBE SHE DOESN'T
HIT HIM ALL THE TIME.

301
00:10:59,033 --> 00:11:00,701
Ross:
When we first met her

302
00:11:00,743 --> 00:11:01,702
SHE WAS SOAKING.

303
00:11:01,744 --> 00:11:03,037
HER FEET WERE WET.

304
00:11:03,079 --> 00:11:04,623
WHO WOULDN'T BE MISERABLE?

305
00:11:04,664 --> 00:11:07,292
I'M TELLING YOU, ONCE I GOT HER
INTO A DRY PAIR OF SHOES

306
00:11:07,334 --> 00:11:09,127
SHE WAS
A TOTALLY DIFFERENT PERSON.

307
00:11:09,169 --> 00:11:10,545
ROSS, COME QUICKLY.

308
00:11:10,587 --> 00:11:12,880
A DEER'S OUTSIDE,
EATING FRUIT FROM THE ORCHARD.

309
00:11:12,922 --> 00:11:15,758
THERE'S A DEER
OUTSIDE, EATING FRUIT
FROM THE ORCHARD.

310
00:11:18,886 --> 00:11:20,263
HE HAD TO GO.

311
00:11:20,305 --> 00:11:23,308
THERE WAS A DEER JUST OUTSIDE,
EATING FRUIT

312
00:11:23,350 --> 00:11:24,309
FROM THE ORCHARD.

313
00:11:24,351 --> 00:11:25,644
I DON'T GET THIS.

314
00:11:25,684 --> 00:11:27,061
SHE WAS HORRIBLE.

315
00:11:27,103 --> 00:11:29,523
OKAY, I'M GOING
TO GO STAND OVER THERE.

316
00:11:30,982 --> 00:11:32,691
WHY DO YOU CARE
SO MUCH ANYWAY?

317
00:11:32,733 --> 00:11:34,653
I DON'T CARE.

318
00:11:34,693 --> 00:11:35,945
YOU KNOW WHAT?

319
00:11:35,987 --> 00:11:37,197
I'M JUST UPSET

320
00:11:37,238 --> 00:11:38,865
THAT I'M GETTING NOWHERE
WITH JOSHUA

321
00:11:38,906 --> 00:11:40,074
THAT... YOU KNOW WHAT?

322
00:11:40,116 --> 00:11:41,909
STILL, YOU DO NOT
JUST MEET SOMEONE

323
00:11:41,951 --> 00:11:43,537
AND GO FLITTING OFF
TO VERMONT.

324
00:11:43,578 --> 00:11:47,332
WELL, WHEN YOU FIRST MET BARRY,
YOU FLITTED OFF TO VAIL.

325
00:11:47,374 --> 00:11:52,504
OH, WOULD YOU JUST FOR ONCE
NOT REMEMBER EVERY LITTLE
THING?

326
00:11:54,839 --> 00:11:57,967
SO, YOU KNOW, UH,
WHEN'S HE GETTING BACK?

327
00:11:58,009 --> 00:11:59,052
COUPLE OF DAYS.

328
00:11:59,093 --> 00:12:00,136
YOU KNOW WHAT?

329
00:12:00,178 --> 00:12:01,262
I KNEW SOMETHING

330
00:12:01,304 --> 00:12:02,972
LIKE THIS WAS
GOING TO HAPPEN

331
00:12:03,014 --> 00:12:04,558
WHAT ARE YOU DOING?

332
00:12:04,599 --> 00:12:05,559
CHANDLER...

333
00:12:05,600 --> 00:12:07,561
YOU CAN'T JUST GO BACK A PHASE.

334
00:12:07,602 --> 00:12:08,562
YES, YOU CAN.

335
00:12:08,603 --> 00:12:10,104
YOU'RE THINKING ABOUT TIME.

336
00:12:10,146 --> 00:12:11,189
YOU CAN'T

337
00:12:11,231 --> 00:12:13,107
GO BACK IN TIME.

338
00:12:13,149 --> 00:12:14,733
LOOK, WHY DON'T YOU JUST...

339
00:12:14,775 --> 00:12:17,696
WHY DON'T YOU DO YOUR PHASE-TWO
STRIP-CLUB THING WITH US?

340
00:12:17,736 --> 00:12:19,072
COME ON,
WE CAN BE GUYS.

341
00:12:19,113 --> 00:12:21,115
( chuckles ):
NO, YOU CAN'T.

342
00:12:21,157 --> 00:12:22,992
COME ON, LET US BE GUYS.

343
00:12:23,034 --> 00:12:24,994
MAYBE WE WANT TO BE GUYS.

344
00:12:25,036 --> 00:12:27,121
YOU DON'T WANT
TO BE GUYS.

345
00:12:27,163 --> 00:12:29,708
YOU'D BE ALL HAIRY,
AND YOU WON'T LIVE AS LONG.

346
00:12:29,748 --> 00:12:32,043
YOU... WOULD YOU JUST
STOP BEING SUCH A WUSS

347
00:12:32,085 --> 00:12:34,379
AND GET THOSE OFF,
AND YOU COME

348
00:12:34,421 --> 00:12:37,716
WITH US AND WATCH NAKED GIRLS
DANCE AROUND!

349
00:12:39,342 --> 00:12:40,427
OKAY.

350
00:12:42,262 --> 00:12:43,179
I'M SORRY.

351
00:12:43,221 --> 00:12:44,222
COME ON.

352
00:12:48,767 --> 00:12:50,353
HEY. JOEY TRIBBIANI.
I'M HERE.

353
00:12:50,395 --> 00:12:51,605
CALM DOWN,
WE GOT TIME.

354
00:12:51,646 --> 00:12:53,189
WE'RE RUNNING
A LITTLE LATE.

355
00:12:53,231 --> 00:12:54,357
OH.

356
00:12:56,150 --> 00:12:57,527
ALL SET.

357
00:13:00,779 --> 00:13:02,365
Joey:
LOOK AT THAT.

358
00:13:02,407 --> 00:13:05,493
CHARLTON HESTON
EATING A LICORICE WHIP.

359
00:13:05,535 --> 00:13:07,078
YEAH, HE LOVES 'EM.

360
00:13:07,120 --> 00:13:08,705
I'VE NEVER SEEN
HIM WITH...

361
00:13:08,747 --> 00:13:09,706
( sniffs )

362
00:13:09,748 --> 00:13:11,249
( both sniffing )

363
00:13:11,291 --> 00:13:13,042
HEY... WHOA...

364
00:13:13,084 --> 00:13:14,877
YEAH, WHAT THE HELL IS THAT?

365
00:13:14,919 --> 00:13:16,671
WHAT SMELLS SO BAD?

366
00:13:16,713 --> 00:13:18,131
YOU.

367
00:13:18,172 --> 00:13:20,592
OH. I COULD SEE
WHY YOU WOULD THINK THAT

368
00:13:20,634 --> 00:13:21,926
BUT, UH...

369
00:13:21,968 --> 00:13:23,844
ACTUALLY, YOU KNOW
WHO I THINK IT IS?

370
00:13:23,886 --> 00:13:24,971
YOU?

371
00:13:25,012 --> 00:13:26,723
NO, NO, IT'S, UH...

372
00:13:26,765 --> 00:13:27,848
IT'S HESTON.

373
00:13:30,310 --> 00:13:31,269
WHAT?

374
00:13:31,311 --> 00:13:32,687
OH, THE MAN REEKS.

375
00:13:32,729 --> 00:13:34,939
SMELLS LIKE HE WENT
ON A THREE-DAY FISHING TRIP

376
00:13:34,981 --> 00:13:35,940
THEN ATE LICORICE.

377
00:13:35,982 --> 00:13:37,442
THERE'S NO WAY HE SMELLS.

378
00:13:37,484 --> 00:13:40,236
HE'S THE ONLY ONE WITH A
SHOWER IN HIS DRESSING ROOM.

379
00:13:40,278 --> 00:13:41,237
REALLY?

380
00:13:41,279 --> 00:13:42,447
A SHOWER, HUH?

381
00:13:42,489 --> 00:13:45,283
AND, UH, WHICH ROOM
MIGHT THAT BE?

382
00:13:45,325 --> 00:13:47,868
THE ONE WITH
"HESTON" ON IT.

383
00:13:49,704 --> 00:13:51,456
INTERESTING.

384
00:14:02,258 --> 00:14:03,968
HEY...

385
00:14:04,010 --> 00:14:05,637
I GOT SOME ONES.

386
00:14:05,679 --> 00:14:08,306
YOU WANT TO PUT THEM
IN HER PANTIES?

387
00:14:08,348 --> 00:14:10,933
NO, THANKS, MOM.

388
00:14:12,477 --> 00:14:13,812
OH, NO, UM, HI.

389
00:14:13,852 --> 00:14:16,481
THAT, THAT...
UM, YOU HAVE
TO PUT THAT OUT

390
00:14:16,523 --> 00:14:18,274
'CAUSE I'M
PREGNANT, SO...

391
00:14:18,316 --> 00:14:20,318
WELL, MAYBE YOU
AND YOUR BABY

392
00:14:20,360 --> 00:14:22,779
OUGHT TO GO
TO ANOTHER STRIP CLUB.

393
00:14:22,821 --> 00:14:25,699
HA-HA, IT'S NOT
MY BABY, HA-HA-HA.

394
00:14:27,992 --> 00:14:29,452
VERY GOOD, YES.

395
00:14:29,494 --> 00:14:31,120
THAT WAS SO GOOD.

396
00:14:31,162 --> 00:14:33,748
REALLY, REALLY ENJOYED IT.

397
00:14:33,790 --> 00:14:35,958
YOU KNOW, VERY EXOTIC.

398
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:37,627
WELL, I JUST CHECKED
OUR MESSAGES

399
00:14:37,669 --> 00:14:38,919
AND JOSHUA DIDN'T CALL.

400
00:14:38,961 --> 00:14:39,920
YOU WOULD THINK

401
00:14:39,962 --> 00:14:41,297
HE WOULD BE WORRIED

402
00:14:41,339 --> 00:14:43,466
ABOUT ME NOT SHOWING UP
AT HIS CLUB.

403
00:14:43,508 --> 00:14:45,635
AND YOU KNOW WHAT
MAKES IT SO MUCH WORSE?

404
00:14:45,677 --> 00:14:48,471
ROSS IS ALL HAPPY IN VERMONT.

405
00:14:48,513 --> 00:14:51,891
COME ON, LOOK
WHERE YOU ARE.

406
00:14:51,932 --> 00:14:54,728
IF YOU GET A SEC,
ANOTHER ROUND OF DAIQUIRIS.

407
00:14:54,769 --> 00:14:56,855
REMEMBER, UM,
VIRGIN FOR ME, PLEASE.

408
00:14:56,896 --> 00:14:59,148
DON'T LET ME LEAVE
WITHOUT GETTING THE NAME

409
00:14:59,190 --> 00:15:00,358
OF THAT CARPET GUY.

410
00:15:00,400 --> 00:15:02,235
OH, COME ON!

411
00:15:03,152 --> 00:15:04,237
ALL RIGHT,
YOU KNOW WHAT?

412
00:15:04,278 --> 00:15:05,446
I'M JUST GOING TO GO HOME
AND CALL KATHY.

413
00:15:05,488 --> 00:15:07,615
WELL, IF YOU THINK IT'LL HELP.

414
00:15:07,657 --> 00:15:09,242
NO, THAT WAS A TEST.

415
00:15:09,283 --> 00:15:11,994
IN A COUPLE HOURS, I'LL GET
REALLY DRUNK AND WANT TO CALL.

416
00:15:12,036 --> 00:15:13,538
YOU GUYS HAVE TO STOP ME.

417
00:15:13,580 --> 00:15:16,374
AND THEN AFTER THAT, I'M GOING
TO WANT TO CALL JANICE.

418
00:15:16,416 --> 00:15:17,542
YOU SHOULD. HOW IS SHE?

419
00:15:17,584 --> 00:15:18,292
OH!

420
00:15:19,960 --> 00:15:22,714
I THINK SOMEBODY NEEDS
ANOTHER LAP DANCE.

421
00:15:22,756 --> 00:15:24,924
( imitating pistol firing )

422
00:15:33,600 --> 00:15:35,685
( door slams )

423
00:15:39,898 --> 00:15:40,899
HELLO?

424
00:15:40,939 --> 00:15:42,233
WHO'S IN THERE?

425
00:15:47,655 --> 00:15:49,574
HOW YOU DOING?

426
00:15:49,616 --> 00:15:51,534
WHO IN THE HELL ARE YOU?

427
00:15:51,576 --> 00:15:52,577
UH...

428
00:15:52,619 --> 00:15:54,245
I GUESS YOU WOULDN'T
BELIEVE ME

429
00:15:54,287 --> 00:15:56,163
IF I SAID I WAS
KIRK DOUGLAS, HUH?

430
00:15:57,624 --> 00:16:01,210
PUT SOME PANTS ON, KID,
SO I CAN KICK YOUR BUTT.

431
00:16:01,252 --> 00:16:04,464
NO-NO-NO, NO, NO, WAIT,
YOU DON'T UNDERSTAND.

432
00:16:04,505 --> 00:16:08,342
SEE, I'M AN ACTOR.

433
00:16:08,384 --> 00:16:09,469
JOEY TRIBBIANI.

434
00:16:09,510 --> 00:16:11,345
I'M DOING A SCENE
WITH YOU TODAY

435
00:16:11,387 --> 00:16:12,764
AND, WELL, I STINK.

436
00:16:12,806 --> 00:16:14,766
YOU'RE IN THIS PICTURE?

437
00:16:14,808 --> 00:16:16,100
YEAH, YEAH.

438
00:16:16,142 --> 00:16:18,269
I'M ONE OF THE COPS
WHO WON'T WORK WITH YOU

439
00:16:18,311 --> 00:16:19,854
'CAUSE YOU'RE A LOOSE CANNON.

440
00:16:19,896 --> 00:16:22,857
ANYWAY, LOOK, I'M REALLY SORRY,
BUT I JUST... I STINK.

441
00:16:24,818 --> 00:16:25,777
JOEY, RIGHT?

442
00:16:25,819 --> 00:16:27,779
YEAH.

443
00:16:27,821 --> 00:16:29,572
COME ON, COME ON.

444
00:16:29,614 --> 00:16:32,241
EVERY ACTOR
AT ONE TIME
OR ANOTHER...

445
00:16:32,283 --> 00:16:33,618
AH!

446
00:16:36,412 --> 00:16:38,539
EVERY ACTOR THINKS HE STINKS.

447
00:16:38,581 --> 00:16:42,209
EVEN LAURENCE OLIVIER
SOMETIMES THOUGHT HE STANK.

448
00:16:42,251 --> 00:16:44,963
BOB REDFORD WON'T EVEN
WATCH HIMSELF.

449
00:16:45,003 --> 00:16:46,172
YOU DON'T UNDERSTAND.

450
00:16:46,213 --> 00:16:47,089
LISTEN TO ME.

451
00:16:47,131 --> 00:16:48,633
OH, YEAH.

452
00:16:48,675 --> 00:16:50,677
I DON'T KNOW ONE ACTOR

453
00:16:50,718 --> 00:16:53,805
WORTH HIS SALT
WHO ONE TIME IN HIS CAREER

454
00:16:53,847 --> 00:16:55,849
DIDN'T SAY, "GOD, I STINK."

455
00:16:55,890 --> 00:16:59,519
HELL, I JUST DID A SCENE
OUT THERE, FIRST TAKE...

456
00:16:59,560 --> 00:17:01,061
I STUNK THE PLACE UP

457
00:17:01,103 --> 00:17:03,481
BUT...

458
00:17:03,523 --> 00:17:04,983
THE IMPORTANT THING

459
00:17:05,023 --> 00:17:06,359
YOU MUST REMEMBER:

460
00:17:06,400 --> 00:17:09,320
NO MATTER HOW BADLY
YOU THINK YOU STINK

461
00:17:09,362 --> 00:17:12,907
YOU MUST NEVER, EVER BUST
INTO MY DRESSING ROOM

462
00:17:12,949 --> 00:17:14,367
AND USE MY SHOWER.

463
00:17:15,952 --> 00:17:17,745
DO YOU UNDERSTAND ME?

464
00:17:17,787 --> 00:17:19,789
YES, SIR. YES, SIR.
I'M-I'M VERY SORRY.

465
00:17:19,831 --> 00:17:20,790
WAIT A MINUTE.

466
00:17:20,832 --> 00:17:21,791
TAKE YOUR PANTS.

467
00:17:21,833 --> 00:17:22,834
YEAH, OH, YEAH.

468
00:17:24,919 --> 00:17:26,420
( chuckles)

469
00:17:26,462 --> 00:17:28,756
SO, WE DID OKAY
AT THE STRIP CLUB, RIGHT?

470
00:17:28,798 --> 00:17:30,257
OH, YEAH,
THAT WAS GREAT.

471
00:17:30,299 --> 00:17:31,759
THANKS TO YOU

472
00:17:31,801 --> 00:17:34,220
THE HOTTEST COCKTAIL WAITRESS
THERE IS QUITTING

473
00:17:34,261 --> 00:17:35,555
TO TEACH THE
THIRD GRADE.

474
00:17:35,596 --> 00:17:36,764
I CAN'T BELIEVE IT.

475
00:17:36,806 --> 00:17:38,057
HE STILL HASN'T CALLED.

476
00:17:38,098 --> 00:17:39,099
WHO? JOSH?

477
00:17:39,141 --> 00:17:40,434
IT'S JOSHUA.

478
00:17:40,476 --> 00:17:41,686
HE DOESN'T LIKE "JOSH"?

479
00:17:41,728 --> 00:17:43,229
NO, I DON'T.

480
00:17:43,270 --> 00:17:45,940
ALL RIGHT, WELL,
I'M GOING TO PUT
MY SWEATS BACK ON.

481
00:17:45,982 --> 00:17:47,107
NO, WAIT, WAIT.

482
00:17:47,149 --> 00:17:48,985
OKAY, YOU KNOW WHAT?
YOU WERE RIGHT.

483
00:17:49,027 --> 00:17:51,153
WE REALLY WEREN'T
GREAT AT BEING GUYS

484
00:17:51,195 --> 00:17:52,363
BUT DO YOU KNOW WHY?

485
00:17:52,405 --> 00:17:53,656
BECAUSE WE'RE GIRLS.

486
00:17:54,824 --> 00:17:55,950
YEAH?

487
00:17:55,992 --> 00:17:57,744
KNOW WHAT GIRLS
ARE REALLY GOOD AT?

488
00:17:57,785 --> 00:17:59,203
STRIPPING.

489
00:18:01,247 --> 00:18:02,707
NO. LISTENING.

490
00:18:02,749 --> 00:18:04,124
SIT.

491
00:18:04,166 --> 00:18:07,628
YOU KNOW, MAYBE JUST
IT WOULD REALLY, REALLY HELP

492
00:18:07,670 --> 00:18:09,380
IF YOU WOULD JUST TALK.

493
00:18:09,422 --> 00:18:10,548
YEAH, COME ON.

494
00:18:10,590 --> 00:18:12,508
WHAT'S GOING
ON IN THERE?

495
00:18:12,550 --> 00:18:15,177
Monica:
YEAH.

496
00:18:15,219 --> 00:18:17,471
AND, YOU KNOW, IF
YOU WANT TO CRY...

497
00:18:17,513 --> 00:18:18,848
THAT'S OKAY, TOO.

498
00:18:18,890 --> 00:18:21,225
OKAY, LOOK,
I'M GOING TO HAVE TO ASK

499
00:18:21,267 --> 00:18:22,602
YOU ALL TO LEAVE.

500
00:18:22,643 --> 00:18:23,686
COME ON,
CHANDLER.

501
00:18:23,728 --> 00:18:25,021
OH, LOOK, FORGET IT.

502
00:18:25,063 --> 00:18:27,815
WE TRIED, BUT PHASE THREE
IS A LOST CAUSE.

503
00:18:27,857 --> 00:18:30,401
OKAY? THOSE STRIPPERS
WERE INSANELY HOT

504
00:18:30,443 --> 00:18:33,571
AND I COULDN'T PICTURE MYSELF
WITH ANY OF THEM.

505
00:18:33,613 --> 00:18:34,781
( sighs )

506
00:18:36,532 --> 00:18:38,492
THEY REALLY
WERE PRETTY,
WEREN'T THEY?

507
00:18:38,534 --> 00:18:39,702
OH...
OOH...

508
00:18:39,744 --> 00:18:42,288
I REALLY LIKED
THAT FIGHTER PILOT ONE.

509
00:18:42,329 --> 00:18:44,707
OH, CANDY? OH,
SHE WAS SO SPUNKY.

510
00:18:44,749 --> 00:18:46,084
YEAH.

511
00:18:46,125 --> 00:18:47,293
YOU KNOW, I THINK

512
00:18:47,334 --> 00:18:49,796
IF I WERE GOING TO
BE WITH A WOMAN...

513
00:18:51,631 --> 00:18:53,633
IT'D BE WITH SOMEONE
LIKE MICHELLE

514
00:18:53,674 --> 00:18:56,260
BECAUSE SHE WAS...
SHE WAS JUST SO PETITE.

515
00:18:56,302 --> 00:18:57,637
SEE, I DON'T KNOW.

516
00:18:57,678 --> 00:18:59,472
FOR ME IT WOULD HAVE
TO BE CHANTAL.

517
00:18:59,513 --> 00:19:00,974
( gasps )
OH, CHANTAL.

518
00:19:01,015 --> 00:19:01,933
YOU KNOW?

519
00:19:01,975 --> 00:19:03,559
OH, MY GOODNESS. OH...

520
00:19:03,601 --> 00:19:05,144
SHE HAD THE SMOOTHEST SKIN.

521
00:19:05,185 --> 00:19:08,272
I MEAN, WHEN I STUFFED THAT
DOLLAR BILL IN HER G-STRING

522
00:19:08,314 --> 00:19:09,649
AND GRAZED HER THIGH...

523
00:19:09,690 --> 00:19:10,984
PHASE THREE!

524
00:19:11,025 --> 00:19:13,736
I JUST ACHIEVED PHASE THREE!

525
00:19:13,778 --> 00:19:15,154
REALLY?

526
00:19:15,195 --> 00:19:17,740
I AM TOTALLY PICTURING YOU
WITH ALL THOSE WOMEN.

527
00:19:17,782 --> 00:19:20,785
THAT'S... THAT'S
NOT PHASE THREE.

528
00:19:20,827 --> 00:19:23,287
WELL, I'M THERE, TOO.

529
00:19:23,329 --> 00:19:26,415
WELL, ARE WE ALL TOGETHER,
LIKE IN A GROUP?

530
00:19:26,457 --> 00:19:27,416
STOP IT!

531
00:19:27,458 --> 00:19:28,626
YOU'RE KILLING ME!

532
00:19:28,668 --> 00:19:30,837
I THINK I JUST MOVED ON
TO PHASE FOUR.

533
00:19:30,878 --> 00:19:32,797
OH, WHAT IS THAT?
WHAT IS THAT?

534
00:19:32,839 --> 00:19:34,214
WHERE I DON'T WANT
TO HAVE A RELATIONSHIP EVER.

535
00:19:34,256 --> 00:19:37,093
I WANT TO HAVE SEX
WITH STRIPPERS
AND MY FRIENDS.

536
00:19:41,179 --> 00:19:42,222
COME ON.

537
00:19:42,264 --> 00:19:44,475
LET ME SEE THAT SMILE.

538
00:19:44,517 --> 00:19:46,185
I DON'T WANT TO.

539
00:19:46,226 --> 00:19:47,979
PLEASE?

540
00:19:48,021 --> 00:19:51,107
I WANTED TO GO
TO THE STRIP CLUB.

541
00:19:51,149 --> 00:19:53,860
I KNOW, BUT YOU'RE GOING
TO HAVE PLENTY OF CHANCES.

542
00:19:53,901 --> 00:19:55,903
THERE ARE THOUSANDS
OF WOMEN OUT THERE

543
00:19:55,945 --> 00:19:57,947
WHO ARE JUST WAITING
TO SCREW ME OVER.

544
00:19:57,989 --> 00:20:00,116
YEAH, ALL RIGHT.

545
00:20:01,159 --> 00:20:03,119
HEY.
HEY.

546
00:20:03,161 --> 00:20:05,204
HEY, OH,
HOW WAS VERMONT?

547
00:20:05,245 --> 00:20:07,665
EMILY IS...

548
00:20:07,707 --> 00:20:08,958
INCREDIBLE.

549
00:20:09,000 --> 00:20:11,502
I MEAN, THERE ARE NO WORDS
TO DESCRIBE HER.

550
00:20:11,544 --> 00:20:15,381
THE WHOLE WEEKEND
WAS, WAS LIKE A DREAM.

551
00:20:15,422 --> 00:20:17,508
OH, AND YOU... RACH.

552
00:20:17,550 --> 00:20:19,010
HEY.

553
00:20:19,052 --> 00:20:21,345
YOU WERE SO RIGHT.

554
00:20:21,387 --> 00:20:22,471
WHAT?

555
00:20:22,513 --> 00:20:23,639
WHAT YOU SAID

556
00:20:23,681 --> 00:20:25,808
ABOUT US FINALLY
BEING IN A PLACE

557
00:20:25,850 --> 00:20:29,103
WHERE WE COULD REALLY
BE HAPPY FOR EACH OTHER.

558
00:20:29,145 --> 00:20:32,565
I MEAN, I... I-I ADMIT
I WASN'T QUITE THERE.

559
00:20:32,606 --> 00:20:34,608
YOU KNOW? I MEAN,
THE THOUGHT

560
00:20:34,650 --> 00:20:37,028
OF YOU AND THAT,
THAT JOSH GUY...

561
00:20:37,070 --> 00:20:37,737
JOSHUA.

562
00:20:37,778 --> 00:20:39,363
JOSHUA... GUY...

563
00:20:39,405 --> 00:20:43,367
AT THAT CLUB, DANCING,
HAVING A GOOD TIME.

564
00:20:43,409 --> 00:20:45,285
THE THOUGHT OF
IT KIND OF...

565
00:20:45,327 --> 00:20:47,038
YOU KNOW?

566
00:20:47,080 --> 00:20:48,164
YEAH...

567
00:20:48,206 --> 00:20:50,124
BUT NOW-- BUT NOW

568
00:20:50,166 --> 00:20:51,667
I'M TOTALLY THERE.

569
00:20:51,709 --> 00:20:53,878
I'M FINALLY
WHERE YOU ARE.

570
00:20:53,920 --> 00:20:55,755
OH, THANK GOODNESS.

571
00:20:55,796 --> 00:20:59,008
YEAH, AND... AND
THANK YOU FOR EMILY.

572
00:20:59,050 --> 00:21:00,384
OH, NO PROBLEM.

573
00:21:00,426 --> 00:21:02,428
I'M SO GLAD I COULD HELP.

574
00:21:02,469 --> 00:21:04,471
YOU KNOW, HAPPY FOR YOU.

575
00:21:04,513 --> 00:21:06,224
HAPPY FOR YOU.

576
00:21:06,264 --> 00:21:07,225
OH, NO.

577
00:21:07,265 --> 00:21:08,893
HAPPY FOR YOU.

578
00:21:14,607 --> 00:21:16,358
HERE'S WHAT WE'RE GOING TO DO.

579
00:21:16,400 --> 00:21:18,318
YOU ARE GOING
TO TAKE OFF MY CLOTHES;

580
00:21:18,360 --> 00:21:20,571
YOU TWO GO GET THE OILS;

581
00:21:20,613 --> 00:21:23,741
AND YOU JUST CONSTANTLY SCREAM
AT THE TOP OF YOUR VOICE

582
00:21:23,783 --> 00:21:27,036
"CHANDLER'S THE KING!
CHANDLER'S THE KING!"

583
00:21:27,078 --> 00:21:28,829
I WANT TO BE WITH HER.

584
00:21:28,871 --> 00:21:29,956
I LIKE HER.

585
00:21:29,997 --> 00:21:31,082
OH, THAT'S FINE.

586
00:21:31,124 --> 00:21:32,499
GO WITH YOUR INSTINCTS.

587
00:21:32,541 --> 00:21:33,793
WHAT AM I DOING AGAIN?

588
00:21:33,834 --> 00:21:34,794
WOULD YOU PLEASE

589
00:21:34,835 --> 00:21:35,836
PAY ATTENTION?

590
00:21:35,878 --> 00:21:37,504
I COULD WAKE UP
AT ANY MOMENT.

591
00:21:37,546 --> 00:21:39,715
I'M JOSHUA. I'M HERE
TO PICK UP RACHEL.

592
00:21:39,757 --> 00:21:41,759
NO, NO. THAT'S
NOT JOSHUA.

593
00:21:41,801 --> 00:21:43,427
WHAT DO YOU
WANT FROM ME?

594
00:21:43,469 --> 00:21:44,804
I NEVER MET THE GUY.

595
00:21:44,845 --> 00:21:47,848
SO, ANYWAY, RACHEL, I'M
SORRY YOU CAN'T STAY.

596
00:21:47,890 --> 00:21:49,225
THE REST OF US HAVE

597
00:21:49,267 --> 00:21:51,018
A LOT OF WORK TO DO.

598
00:21:52,645 --> 00:21:55,397
[Captioned by
The Caption Center
WGBH Educational Foundation]

599
00:21:55,439 --> 00:21:57,150
WHAT ARE YOU DOING?

600
00:21:57,191 --> 00:21:59,235
ALL RIGHT, LISTEN,
I GOT TO WAKE UP.

